    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170-a2">

                <pb facs="0440" n="350" xml:id="pg350"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in inclosure 1 in No.
                    70.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Taotai at Tien-tsin to Mr. Sheppard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tien-tsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 19,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have already appointed deputies to sit
                    conjointly with you in the trial of the collision case between the junk Chin I
                    Hung and the American steamer Shantung; but on considering the unusual gravity
                    of this case—the serious damage to the junk and the large quantity of rice
                    involved—I wished to go in person and sit with you, but I cannot arrange to
                    leave my business, which is very pressing just now. I have therefore requested
                    Mr. Twinem, acting commissioner of customs, to appear at your consulate
                    to-morrow morning, at 10 o’clock, and represent me in acting conjointly with you
                    in the hearing of this case, in order that a due regard may be shown for im
                    portant business.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>Cards and compliments of</p>
                <closer><signed>CUSTOMS TAOTAI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eli T. Sheppard</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul, &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
